![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The current `sed` range match `/^ensure_trailing_newline() {/,/^}/p` is fragile because it will prematurely terminate if any line inside the function starts with a closing brace `}` (for example, inside a nested block, multi-line statement, or if the code is reformatted).

To make the function extraction robust and independent of Python, we can use `awk` to perform brace depth counting. This matches the logic of the original Python implementation while remaining lightweight and portable.

```suggestion
	awk '
	/^ensure_trailing_newline\(\) [{]/ { collect = 1 }
	collect {
		print
		depth += gsub(/[{]/, "{") - gsub(/[}]/, "}")
		if (depth == 0 && $0 ~ /^[[:space:]]*[}]/) {
			exit
		}
	}
	' "$REPO_DIR/aidevops.sh"
```

