![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Add a defensive guard at the beginning of the handler to ensure `client?.session?.update` is a function before executing any logic. This prevents runtime `TypeError`s if the client or its session update API is not available. Since this guard is in place, we can also simplify the `catch` block by removing the redundant `client?.session?.update` check.

```javascript
export function createSessionTitleSuffixHandler({ agentsDir, client }) {
  const inFlight = new Set();

  return async function sessionTitleSuffixHandler(input) {
    if (typeof client?.session?.update !== "function") return;

    const eventType = input?.event?.type || input?.type || "";
    if (eventType !== "session.updated") return;

    const info = getEventInfo(input);
    const title = info?.title || "";
    if (!title) return;

    const version = readAidevopsVersion(agentsDir);
    const suffixedTitle = withAidevopsTitleSuffix(title, version);
    if (suffixedTitle === title) return;

    const sessionID = getEventSessionId(input, info);
    if (!sessionID || inFlight.has(sessionID)) return;

    inFlight.add(sessionID);
    try {
      try {
        await client.session.update({
          path: { id: sessionID },
          body: { title: suffixedTitle },
        });
      } catch (err) {
        await client.session.update({
          path: { sessionID },
          body: { title: suffixedTitle },
        });
      }
    } finally {
      inFlight.delete(sessionID);
    }
  };
}
```

