![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

There is a subtle but significant issue with the test helper `withTempAgentsDir` (and similarly `withoutEnvVersion`) when used with asynchronous test functions.

Because `withTempAgentsDir` is a synchronous function and does not `await` the promise returned by `fn(dir)`, its `finally` block executes immediately after `fn(dir)` is called (as soon as it returns a pending promise). This means the temporary directory is deleted **before** any asynchronous operations inside the test have finished executing.

Currently, the tests only pass because all file reads/writes and mock client operations happen to run synchronously before the first `await` suspension point. If any of these operations are refactored to be asynchronous in the future, the tests will fail because the directory will have already been cleaned up.

To fix this, both `withTempAgentsDir` and `withoutEnvVersion` should be refactored to be `async` functions that `await` the callback:

```javascript
async function withTempAgentsDir(fn) {
  const root = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), "aidevops-title-suffix-"));
  const dir = join(root, "agents");
  mkdirSync(dir);
  try {
    return await fn(dir);
  } finally {
    rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });
  }
}

async function withoutEnvVersion(fn) {
  const saved = process.env.AIDEVOPS_VERSION;
  try {
    delete process.env.AIDEVOPS_VERSION;
    return await fn();
  } finally {
    if (saved === undefined) delete process.env.AIDEVOPS_VERSION;
    else process.env.AIDEVOPS_VERSION = saved;
  }
}
```

