body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `.git/config` parser does not reset `currentRemote` when entering other non-remote sections (such as `[branch "main"]` or `[core]`). If any of those subsequent sections contain a `url` key, it will be incorrectly parsed and attributed to the last seen remote. Resetting `currentRemote` when encountering any other section header avoids this misattribution.

```typescript
  const remotes: GuiLocalRepoSetupSummary["remotes"] = [];
  let currentRemote = "";
  for (const line of config.split("\n")) {
    const section = line.match(/^\s*\[remote\s+"([^"]+)"\]\s*$/);
    if (section !== null) {
      currentRemote = section[1];
      continue;
    }
    if (line.match(/^\s*\[/)) {
      currentRemote = "";
      continue;
    }
    const url = line.match(/^\s*url\s*=\s*(.+)\s*$/);
    if (url !== null && currentRemote.length > 0) {
      remotes.push({ name: currentRemote, url_ref: sanitizeRemoteUrl(url[1]) });
    }
  }
  return remotes;
```

