The parser logic in `packages/gui-api/src/status-adapter.ts` has been updated to correctly reset `currentRemote` when encountering non-remote section headers. This prevents subsequent `url` keys from being incorrectly attributed to the previous remote. Thank you for verifying the fix in the current branch.

```suggestion
  for (const line of config.split("\n")) {
    const section = line.match(/^\s*\[remote\s+"([^"]+)"\]\s*$/);
    if (section !== null) {
      currentRemote = section[1];
      continue;
    }
    if (line.match(/^\s*\[/) !== null) {
      currentRemote = "";
      continue;
    }
    const url = line.match(/^\s*url\s*=\s*(.+)\s*$/);
    if (url !== null && currentRemote.length > 0) {
      remotes.push({ name: currentRemote, url_ref: sanitizeRemoteUrl(url[1]) });
    }
  }
