![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

### Robustness Issue: Unhandled `ValueError` / `TypeError` in `last_state`

`last_state` converts the sequence number of the last record to an integer using `int(last[FIELD_SEQUENCE])`. If the log file is corrupted or tampered with such that the sequence is not a valid integer, this will cause `cmd_append` to crash with a traceback.

### Recommendation
Wrap the integer conversion in a `try...except` block and raise a clean `AuditError`.

```suggestion
def last_state(records: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> tuple[int, str]:
    if not records:
        return 0, GENESIS_HASH
    last = records[-1]
    try:
        seq = int(last[FIELD_SEQUENCE])
    except (ValueError, TypeError) as exc:
        raise AuditError(ERR_CORRUPTED, "Vault audit sequence in last record is not a valid integer", 3) from exc
    return seq, str(last[FIELD_RECORD_HASH])
```

