`navigator.clipboard.writeText` is an asynchronous operation that can fail and throw an error (e.g., in non-secure contexts, or if the document lacks focus). Since the promise is discarded with `void`, any rejection will result in an unhandled promise rejection. We should wrap it in a `try...catch` block to handle potential clipboard write errors gracefully.

```
async function copyCurrentSurfaceLink(surface: SurfaceId): Promise<void> {
  const browserUrl = typeof window === "undefined" ? "" : window.location.href.split("#")[0];
  const link = browserUrl.length > 0 ? `${browserUrl}#surface=${surface}` : `aidevops://surface/${surface}`;

  if (typeof navigator !== "undefined" && navigator.clipboard) {
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(link);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error("Failed to copy link to clipboard:", error);
    }
  }
}
```

