![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Process stdout and stderr are streams that emit arbitrary chunks of data, which are not guaranteed to be aligned with line endings. Splitting raw chunks directly can result in fragmented lines. Use Node's built-in `readline` module to correctly buffer and parse complete lines, and add null checks for safety.

```suggestion
  if (child.stdout) {
    const rlStdout = readline.createInterface({ input: child.stdout, terminal: false });
    rlStdout.on("line", (line) => appendJobLine(job, line));
  }
  if (child.stderr) {
    const rlStderr = readline.createInterface({ input: child.stderr, terminal: false });
    rlStderr.on("line", (line) => appendJobLine(job, line));
  }
```

