The `selectedJob` object reference changes on every poll response because the `jobs` state is updated. Since `selectedJob` is in the dependency array of `useEffect`, the interval is cleared and recreated on every single poll, which can cause erratic timing. Depend on `selectedJobId` and the job's status string instead to ensure a stable interval.

```suggestion
  useEffect(() => {
    const jobStatus = selectedJobId ? jobs[selectedJobId]?.status : null;
    if (selectedJobId === null || jobStatus !== "running") {
      return undefined;
    }

    const timer = window.setInterval(() => {
      void refreshJob(selectedJobId, setJobs);
    }, 1_500);

    return () => window.clearInterval(timer);
  }, [selectedJobId, jobs[selectedJobId]?.status]);
```

