![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

Changing the default `.chat-composer` grid template to three columns (`auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto`) breaks the layout of the standard chat composer in `ConversationWorkspace` (People chat), which only has two children (`textarea` and `button`). This causes the `textarea` to shrink to `auto` and the "Send" button to expand to fill the remaining space.

To fix this, keep the default `.chat-composer` as a two-column grid and introduce a specific modifier class (e.g., `.ai-composer`) for the three-column layout.

```suggestion
.chat-composer {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  display: grid;
