![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

### Range Slider Label Alignment Mismatch

By removing the `:first-child` and `:last-child` text alignment rules for `.range-labels button`, the first ("xs") and last ("xl") labels are now centered within their respective grid columns.

Since the slider track spans 100% of the width, centering these labels causes them to be visually misaligned with the start and end points of the slider track:
- The "xs" label is shifted too far to the right.
- The "xl" label is shifted too far to the left.

#### Recommendation
Restore the `text-align: left` for the first button and `text-align: right` for the last button to ensure they align perfectly with the edges of the slider track.

```css
.range-labels button {
  background: transparent;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 8px;
  color: inherit;
  font: inherit;
  padding: 2px 0;
  text-align: center;
}

.range-labels button:first-child {
  text-align: left;
}

.range-labels button:last-child {
  text-align: right;
}

.range-labels button:hover,
.range-labels button:focus-visible,
.range-labels .active {
  color: var(--accent);
  outline: none;
}
```

