When reading from a stream that may be chunked incrementally, it is recommended to set `crlfDelay: Infinity` in `readline.createInterface`. This ensures that if a carriage return (`\r`) and a newline (`\n`) are split across chunk boundaries (even with a delay), they are still correctly treated as a single line ending rather than two separate line endings.

