When `process.env.HOME` is undefined, `home` defaults to an empty string `""`. Joining an empty string with paths like `".bun/bin"` results in relative paths being added to the `PATH` environment variable. This can lead to untrusted search path vulnerabilities (CWE-426) or unexpected behavior depending on the current working directory. Only append home-relative paths to `extraPaths` if `HOME` is actually defined.

```typescript
function expandedPath(): string {
  const home = process.env.HOME;
  const extraPaths = [
    "/opt/homebrew/bin",
    "/usr/local/bin",
    "/usr/bin",
    "/bin",
    "/usr/sbin",
    "/sbin",
  ];
  if (home) {
    extraPaths.push(
      join(home, ".bun/bin"),
      join(home, ".local/bin"),
      join(home, ".cursor/bin"),
      join(home, ".qlty/bin")
    );
  }
  return [...new Set([...(process.env.PATH ?? "").split(":"), ...extraPaths].filter(Boolean))].join(":");
}
```

