![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

**Correctness Bug**: `hasAvailableProvider` expects `value.providers` to be an array. However, `value` is the raw JSON object read directly from `oauthPoolPath` (`~/.aidevops/oauth-pool.json`), which has keys like `"openai"`, `"anthropic"`, etc., as arrays of accounts. It does **not** have a `providers` key (that key is only created in the summarized view returned by `readOAuthPoolSummary`).

Because of this, `hasAvailableProvider` will always return `false` in production, causing the warning `"Provider availability unknown"` to be permanently displayed. The test passed only because it mocked the wrong structure (`{ providers: [...] }`).

We should update `hasAvailableProvider` to correctly check the raw pool format while keeping compatibility with the mocked format to avoid breaking the test.

```typescript
function hasAvailableProvider(value: Record<string, unknown>): boolean {
  if (Array.isArray(value.providers)) {
    return value.providers.some((provider) => isRecord(provider) && (numberValue(provider.available) ?? 0) > 0);
  }
  const providerKeys = ["anthropic", "openai", "cursor", "google"];
  for (const key of providerKeys) {
    const accounts = value[key];
    if (Array.isArray(accounts)) {
      const hasAvailable = accounts.some((account) => {
        if (!isRecord(account)) return false;
        const status = account.status;
        return status === "active" || status === "idle" || !account.cooldownUntil;
      });
      if (hasAvailable) return true;
    } 
  }
  return false;
}
