![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Similar to `readJsonLines`, if any single `report.json` file is malformed or unreadable, the entire `readTokenReports` function will fail and discard all other valid reports.

Wrapping the individual file read and parse in a `try-catch` block ensures that one corrupted report doesn't prevent the successful loading of the remaining valid reports.

Additionally, when listing directories, we should use `statSync(path).isDirectory()` instead of `entry.isDirectory()` from `readdirSync(..., { withFileTypes: true })` to ensure symbolic links are correctly followed.

```typescript
function readTokenReports(root: string): { health: "present" | "missing" | "invalid"; records: MetricRecord[] } {
  if (!existsSync(root)) {
    return { health: "missing", records: [] };
  }
  try {
    const paths = readdirSync(root)
      .map((name) => join(root, name))
      .filter((pathName) => {
        try {
          return statSync(pathName).isDirectory();
        } catch {
          return false;
        }
      })
      .map((dir) => join(dir, "report.json"))
      .filter((pathName) => existsSync(pathName))
      .slice(-25);
    const records: MetricRecord[] = [];
    for (const pathName of paths) {
      try {
        const parsed = JSON.parse(readFileSync(pathName, "utf8"));
        if (isRecord(parsed)) {
          records.push(parsed);
        }
      } catch {
        // Ignore malformed report files to ensure robustness
      }
    }
    return { health: "present", records };
  } catch {
    return { health: "invalid", records: [] };
  }
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When listing directories in Node.js and symbolic links need to be followed, use `statSync(path).isDirectory()` instead of `entry.isDirectory()` from `readdirSync(..., { withFileTypes: true })`, as the latter does not resolve symlinks.
</details>

