![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

### Performance Optimization

`recordTimeMs` parses dates and loops over keys. Currently, `filterWindow` is called multiple times (twice in `readPulseWorkersSummary` and four times in `buildCharts`), meaning `recordTimeMs` is called up to 6 times per record. For large telemetry files, this will cause significant performance degradation.

We can optimize this by using a `WeakMap` to cache the parsed timestamp for each `MetricRecord` object. This is completely self-contained and requires zero changes to any caller signatures.

```typescript
const timestampCache = new WeakMap<MetricRecord, number | null>();

function recordTimeMs(record: MetricRecord): number | null {
  const cached = timestampCache.get(record);
  if (cached !== undefined) {
    return cached;
  }
  let result: number | null = null;
  for (const key of ["ts", "timestamp", "started_at", "finished_at", "created_at", "updated_at"]) {
    const value = record[key];
    if (typeof value === "number" && Number.isFinite(value)) {
      result = value > 9_999_999_999 ? value : value * 1000;
      break;
    }
    if (typeof value === "string" && value.length > 0) {
      const parsed = Date.parse(value);
      if (Number.isFinite(parsed)) {
        result = parsed;
        break;
      }
    }
  }
  timestampCache.set(record, result);
  return result;
}
```

