![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The newly introduced multi-layered radial and linear gradients on the `body` selector use hardcoded dark HSL values (e.g., lightness values of `11%` to `22%`). Because `body` is a global selector, these dark gradients will also be applied in the light theme (`data-theme="light"`), resulting in dark/muddy background patches that severely degrade contrast and readability for the dark text (`--text-primary: #111111`).

To preserve the light theme's appearance and readability, scope this dark gradient background specifically to the dark theme (using `[data-theme="dark"] body`), while keeping a light-friendly background (like the original one) for the light theme.

```css
  background:
    radial-gradient(ellipse at top left, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, transparent) 0%, transparent 36%),
    var(--bg-secondary);
  background-attachment: fixed;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  color: var(--text-primary);
  font-family: var(--font-family-app);
  line-height: 1.6;
  margin: 0;
  min-height: 100vh;
  font-size: var(--font-size-app);
}

[data-theme="dark"] body {
  background:
    radial-gradient(ellipse 78% 64% at top left,
      hsl(var(--accent-hue) 96% 22% / 62%) 0%,
      hsl(var(--accent-hue) 92% 18% / 34%) 34%,
      transparent 58%),
    radial-gradient(ellipse 72% 62% at bottom right,
      hsl(var(--accent-hue) 90% 16% / 38%) 0%,
      hsl(var(--accent-hue) 84% 12% / 20%) 38%,
