body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Using the nullish coalescing operator (`??`) allows empty strings (e.g., `?tenant_ref=`) to bypass the fallback and result in empty scope identifiers. This can lead to malformed thread keys (e.g., `::conversation:local`) and potential key collisions or scope validation bypasses.

Using the logical OR operator (`||`) ensures that empty strings correctly fall back to their default values. Additionally, applying the fallback after `threadScopeRef` ensures that inputs that become empty after stripping colons (e.g., `:::`) also fall back safely.

```suggestion
    const tenantRef = threadScopeRef(context.req.query("tenant_ref") ?? "local") || "local";
    const workspaceRef = threadScopeRef(context.req.query("workspace_ref") ?? "aidevops") || "aidevops";
    const sessionRef = context.req.query("session_ref") || "conversation:local";
```

